title: Genesis 8 – While the Earth Remaineth
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 8: the waters abate, the ark rests, the raven and the dove, Noah’s altar, and God’s promise that seedtime and harvest shall not cease.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-8-while-the-earth-remaineth.html

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5): verse slides are kicker "vv." -> sub -> passage -> one paragraph; cross
# references are fig cards. Slide text is the author's own sentences from the Genesis 8 study (posts 6605, 6606).

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 8 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 8: While the Earth Remaineth
sub: The Waters Abate • The Altar • Seedtime and Harvest
refs: Genesis 8:1-22
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The waters abate
--- God Remembered Noah
kicker: vv. 1–3
sub: The Fountains of the Deep and the Windows of Heaven Stopped
scripture: Genesis 8:1-3 | mark: God remembered Noah; The fountains also of the deep and the windows of heaven were stopped
p: Noah and his ark of survivors ride out the flood, and the deluge abates, as God closes up the windows of heaven and the fountains of the deep. [[Genesis 7:11]]

--- The Ark Rested
kicker: vv. 4–5
sub: Upon the Mountains of Ararat
scripture: Genesis 8:4-5 | mark: the ark rested in the seventh month, on the seventeenth day of the month, upon the mountains of Ararat
p: The final resting place for the ark, in Turkey: Mt. Ararat. So many “In Search Of”s and History channel specials claim to have found the ark, but we know everything we need to from scripture.

--- The Raven and the Dove
kicker: vv. 6–9
sub: The Dove Found No Rest for the Sole of Her Foot
scripture: Genesis 8:6-9

--- An Olive Leaf Pluckt Off
kicker: vv. 10–12
sub: Nothing Is Incidental in Scripture
scripture: Genesis 8:10-12 | mark: in her mouth was an olive leaf pluckt off
p: The raven and the doves sent by Noah, and the olive branch the dove returns with, are taught in every Sunday school: that God offered an olive branch of peace to mankind. It reads a bit more into it than is there, but maybe. Nothing is incidental, accidental or coincidental in scripture.

--- The Six Hundredth and First Year
kicker: vv. 13–14
sub: A Hard Record of Events
scripture: Genesis 8:13-14 | mark: in the six hundredth and first year
p: Noah’s 601st birthday is marked while waiting to get God’s blessing to disembark. The times given are details that mark this account as historical rather than symbolic or allegory. God rarely gives precise measures of time or place unless it is to create a hard record of events in scripture. So we know the days and the weeks and the months of the flood and the aftermath.

--- Go Forth of the Ark
kicker: vv. 15–19
sub: Be Fruitful, and Multiply upon the Earth
scripture: Genesis 8:15-19 | mark: Go forth of the ark

=== A sweet savour
--- Noah Builded an Altar
kicker: v. 20
sub: Of Every Clean Beast, and of Every Clean Fowl
scripture: Genesis 8:20 | mark: Noah builded an altar unto the LORD
p: Noah settled in, the ark unloaded, makes sacrifice to God. An act of incredible faith, given the limited number of animals to survive the flood, and it is pleasing unto God. [[Genesis 7:2-3]]

--- The {Lord} Smelled a Sweet Savour
kicker: vv. 21–22
sub: While the Earth Remaineth
scripture: Genesis 8:21-22 | mark: the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth; While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night shall not cease
p: God gives us insight to His thought process, recognizing the evil imagination within man’s heart, and vows never to destroy every living thing because of it. Rather than curse the ground and total destruction of life, God vows to preserve the world as is until the end.

--- The Imagination of Man’s Heart
kicker: Cross references • Genesis 8:21
fig: Genesis 6:5 | Genesis 6:5 | The same evil imagination of man’s heart that God saw before the flood. God does not vow to preserve the world because man is better, but because He has promised.
fig: Genesis 9:11 | Genesis 9:11 | We will see the covenant with Noah God gives in [[lesson:genesis-9-blessings-and-covenant|Genesis 9]].

=== Seedtime and harvest
--- Environmentalist Panic
kicker: Application • Genesis 8:22
sub: Seedtime and Harvest Shall Not Cease
p: This is why environmentalist panic is unbiblical nonsense. We are not going to see cataclysmic climate change of any type before the day of the {Lord}.
callout: I wonder sometimes if the entire point of climate panic is to make those alive during the tribulation and into the wrath of God doubt His hand in it. I think it’s foolish cope, but there probably will be some deluded souls, even as the locusts of Hell bite them in the darkness, blaming CO₂ emissions. [[Revelation 9:2-6]]

--- While the Earth Remaineth
center: Noah gave thanks on dry ground, and God promised: while the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night shall not cease. God will preserve the world as is until the end. [[Genesis 8:22]]
